Relevant columns and their potential usage
• SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02  
  – "project_short_name": filter to the TCGA‑BLCA project  
  – "Hugo_Symbol": locate mutations in CDKN2A  
  – "case_barcode": connect mutations to the same patient in the other tables  
  – "sample_barcode_tumor": connect to RNA samples, if desired  
  – "Variant_Classification", "Variant_Type": optional mutation details  

• RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39  
  – "project_short_name": filter to TCGA‑BLCA  
  – "gene_name": pull the four genes of interest (MDM2, TP53, CDKN1A, CCNE1)  
  – "case_barcode": join back to mutation & clinical tables  
  – "sample_type_name": keep only “Primary Tumor” (or inspect values first)  
  – "fpkm_uq_unstranded", "tpm_unstranded": typical expression measures  

• CLINICAL_GDC_R39  
  – "proj__project_id": filter to TCGA‑BLCA  
  – "submitter_id" ≙ TCGA case barcode: join to mutation / RNA tables  
  – Selected clinical descriptors, e.g. "primary_site", "disease_type", "diag__ajcc_pathologic_stage", "demo__gender", "demo__race", …  

Typical conditions  
• "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'  (RNA, mutation)  
• "proj__project_id" = 'TCGA-BLCA'    (clinical)  
• "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'            (mutation filter)  
• "gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')  (RNA)  
• "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%'        (RNA – restrict to tumor samples)  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that gradually build toward the final integrated view.  
All identifiers are double‑quoted; no schema/type discovery queries are included.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Look at which genes are mutated in TCGA‑BLCA (quick sanity check)
SELECT DISTINCT "Hugo_Symbol"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect CDKN2A mutations in bladder cancer
SELECT  "case_barcode",
        "sample_barcode_tumor",
        "Variant_Classification",
        "Variant_Type",
        "Start_Position",
        "End_Position"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Obtain the list of distinct cases (patients) that carry CDKN2A mutations
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Preview available RNA‑seq sample types for TCGA‑BLCA
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_type_name"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Inspect raw RNA‑seq expression rows for the gene TP53
SELECT  "case_barcode",
        "sample_barcode",
        "gene_name",
        "tpm_unstranded",
        "fpkm_uq_unstranded"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "gene_name" = 'TP53'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Retrieve RNA expression of the four genes in BLCA primary‑tumor samples
SELECT  "case_barcode",
        "sample_barcode",
        "gene_name",
        "tpm_unstranded",
        "fpkm_uq_unstranded"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND "gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
  AND "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Join CDKN2A‑mutant case list with RNA expression for the four genes
WITH cdkn2a_cases AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
  FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
  WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
    AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT  r."case_barcode",
        r."sample_barcode",
        r."gene_name",
        r."tpm_unstranded",
        r."fpkm_uq_unstranded"
FROM cdkn2a_cases c
JOIN TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39 r
      ON r."case_barcode" = c."case_barcode"
WHERE r."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND r."gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
  AND r."sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Preview clinical information fields available for BLCA patients
SELECT  "submitter_id",
        "primary_site",
        "disease_type",
        "diag__ajcc_pathologic_stage",
        "demo__gender",
        "demo__race"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.CLINICAL_GDC_R39
WHERE "proj__project_id" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Combine CDKN2A‑mutant cases with selected clinical data
WITH cdkn2a_cases AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
  FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
  WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
    AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT  clin."submitter_id"  AS "case_barcode",
        clin."primary_site",
        clin."disease_type",
        clin."diag__ajcc_pathologic_stage",
        clin."demo__gender",
        clin."demo__race"
FROM cdkn2a_cases m
JOIN TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.CLINICAL_GDC_R39 clin
      ON clin."submitter_id" = m."case_barcode"
WHERE clin."proj__project_id" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final integrated view – RNA expression & clinical data for CDKN2A‑mutant BLCA cases
WITH cdkn2a_cases AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
  FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.SOMATIC_MUTATION_HG19_MC3_2017_02
  WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
    AND "Hugo_Symbol" = 'CDKN2A'
)
SELECT  r."case_barcode",
        r."sample_barcode",
        r."gene_name",
        r."tpm_unstranded",
        r."fpkm_uq_unstranded",
        clin."primary_site",
        clin."disease_type",
        clin."diag__ajcc_pathologic_stage",
        clin."demo__gender",
        clin."demo__race"
FROM cdkn2a_cases m
JOIN TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R39 r
      ON r."case_barcode" = m."case_barcode"
JOIN TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.CLINICAL_GDC_R39 clin
      ON clin."submitter_id" = r."case_barcode"
WHERE r."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND clin."proj__project_id" = 'TCGA-BLCA'
  AND r."gene_name" IN ('MDM2','TP53','CDKN1A','CCNE1')
  AND r."sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Primary%Tumor%'
LIMIT 20;
```

